  "scope": [
    "Remove patch/file/index/hunk metadata from displayed source rows. Prefer complete ordinary source context; count and navigate actual change blocks, including multiple blocks inside one full-context hunk.",
    "Keep row/output/line limits. Only resourceBudget retries once with four context lines, replacing the first option without changing literal filenames; omitted context is explicit. Staged HEAD is fixed, and index/disk verification remains after projection.",
    "Place version/path/selection headers inside native diff panes so they follow divider widths; remove the extra path bar. Full-row/gutter backgrounds and visible contiguous block connectors share the source row geometry.",
    "Quiet outlined search fields; collapse commit path search by default, group visible changes and show filename status. Extend message area and keep actions at the bottom, preserving low-height scrolling and native message undo.",
    "Keep remote configuration issues in the remote warning entry and settings, leaving real status/write failures visible. No remote/authentication/execution policy is relaxed.",
    "Open local and remote branch groups by default, group remote names, use muted graph color, compact log filters and persistent split file/detail empty states.",
    "Suggest 380pt only for the first bottom Git display when the bottom divider has not been manually adjusted. Other tool defaults and saved internal ratios remain intact."
  ],
